---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = 'October 18, 2026';
---
<Base title="Terms of Use" description="Terms for using Load Plan Calc and its calculators.">
  <section>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="small">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <p class="lede">By using this site you agree to these terms.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Information only</h2>
    <p>Load Plan Calc provides load planning calculators and general reference information. Plans are estimates: real loads depend on the exact container or vehicle, carton bulge, dunnage and securing, and errors can occur. Check sizes and weight limits with your carrier, follow the securing and weight rules that apply to your shipment, and do not exceed any vehicle, container or road limit.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>The site and its tools are provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any loss or damage arising from use of the site.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Trademarks</h2>
    <p>Product and brand names mentioned on this site are trademarks of their owners and are used only to identify products. We are not affiliated with or endorsed by any carrier, container owner or manufacturer.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Content</h2>
    <p>Text, tools and design on this site belong to Load Plan Calc. You may link to any page and quote short extracts with a link back.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:contact@loadplancalc.com">contact@loadplancalc.com</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
